@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About Us | Entwined &amp; Unwind</PageTitle>

<div @onkeydown="HandleReviewsKeyDown">
    <button type="button" class="reviews-toggle" aria-expanded="@(reviewsOpen ? "true" : "false")"
            aria-controls="reviews-drawer" @onclick="ToggleReviews" @ref="reviewsToggle">
        Reviews
    </button>
    @if (reviewsOpen)
    {
        <aside id="reviews-drawer" class="reviews-drawer" aria-labelledby="reviews-heading">
            <div class="reviews-header">
                <h2 id="reviews-heading">Reviews &amp; Testimonials</h2>
                <button type="button" class="reviews-close" aria-label="Close reviews" @onclick="CloseReviews" @ref="reviewsClose">&times;</button>
            </div>
            <div class="reviews-content" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Client testimonials">
                @if (testimonials.Length == 0)
                {
                    <p>Client stories will be shared here soon.</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <p><strong>Preview only:</strong> These are fictional sample reviews for testing.</p>
                    @foreach (var testimonial in testimonials)
                    {
                        <figure class="review-card">
                            <blockquote><p>@testimonial.Quote</p></blockquote>
                            <figcaption>@testimonial.Name</figcaption>
                        </figure>
                    }
                }
            </div>
        </aside>
    }
</div>

<section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-navy">About Us</span>
        <h1>Hi, we're so glad you're here.</h1>
        <p>Grounded, intuitive, heart-centered energy healing for your journey back to yourself.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="practitioners">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Meet Your Practitioners</span>
            <h2>The People Behind Your Session</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="practitioners-grid">
            <div class="practitioner-card" id="mary">
                <div class="practitioner-photo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <h3 class="practitioner-name">Mary</h3>
                <span class="practitioner-title">Reiki I &amp; II Therapist &middot; Dynamic Body Balancing Facilitator</span>
                <div class="practitioner-bio">
                    <p>
                        Hi, I'm Mary! I'm a Reiki I &amp; II therapist and Dynamic Body Balancing
                        facilitator with a background in education and a passion for helping
                        others grow, heal, and better understand themselves.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        My own journey has led me to become deeply interested in the connection
                        between our emotions, beliefs, physical bodies, intuition, and overall
                        well-being. I believe that many of the limitations we experience in life
                        are opportunities for growth, and that becoming aware of the emotions and
                        beliefs we carry can help us reconnect with who we truly are.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        As a mother and former educator, caring for and teaching others has
                        always been a big part of who I am. I bring that same caring,
                        open-minded, and nonjudgmental approach into my work. My goal is to
                        create a space where you feel completely comfortable being yourself,
                        opening up, and exploring whatever comes forward.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Through my work, I hope to help others release what may no longer be
                        serving them, challenge limiting beliefs, experience greater relaxation,
                        strengthen their connection with their higher self and intuition, and
                        gain a deeper understanding of themselves and their purpose.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        More than anything, I want every person I work with to leave feeling
                        that our time together made a meaningful difference.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="practitioner-card" id="leslie">
                <div class="practitioner-photo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                <h3 class="practitioner-name">Leslie</h3>
                <span class="practitioner-title">Dynamic Body Balancing Practitioner &middot; Lactation Educator</span>
                <div class="practitioner-bio">
                    <p>
                        Hi, I'm Leslie! I'm a mother of two, a Dynamic Body Balancing
                        practitioner, and a Lactation Educator with a deep passion for helping
                        mothers and children feel more supported, understood, and connected.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        My journey into this work began through motherhood. Having a colicky
                        baby of my own opened my eyes to just how much babies communicate
                        through their bodies and behaviors. I learned firsthand that a baby's
                        cry is not simply something to quiet or ignore&mdash;it is communication.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I'm especially passionate about supporting mothers and children who are
                        struggling with some of the same things I have experienced along my own
                        journey. I believe that mothers deserve to feel heard and supported.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Through my work, my goal is to create a safe, welcoming space where
                        mothers can slow down, reconnect with themselves and their children, and
                        explore what their bodies may be communicating. I hope to help families
                        better understand their experiences and feel more confident in their
                        intuition as parents.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        More than anything, I want the mothers and children I work with to feel
                        that they are not alone&mdash;and that their experiences matter.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

